ENGLISH 10

&
\newpage
\begin{verbatim}
%
% TRANSFORMATION TVPDeletion
< m1: SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}
              [ I1:mu1,
                predrel/VERBP{VERBPrec1}[ ],
                I3:mu3
              ] 
>

< m : SENTENCE{SENTENCErec1}
              [ I1:mu1, 
                I3:mu3 
              ]
>

   MATCHCONDITIONS
      <
       I1 : ALL (mu1, I11:rel1/..)
          I11: rel1 IN AUX_preVPrels
       I3 : ALL (mu3, I13:rel3/..)
          I13: rel3 IN AUX_postVPrels
      >

      COMP
         <
          C1: true
          A1: @
         >

      DECOMP
         <
          C1: true
          A1: @
         >

&

\end{verbatim}
\newpage
\begin{description}
\item[* name:] TVPDeletion
\item[* relevant examples:] where is he $_{VP}$[ ] $\rightarrow$ where is he
\item[* language:] (Dutch, English, Spanish) English
\item[* kind of rule:] (M-rule, S-rule, Transferrule) M-rule
\item[* subgrammar:] CLAUSEtoSENTENCE
\item[* class:] (name of rule, transformation or filter class) TC\_VPDeletion
\item[* date of creation:] 8-SEP-1988
\item[* author:] margreet sanders
\item[* copied from:] Dutch Tvpdel1
\item[* modification:]\mbox{}
\begin{enumerate}
\item date: 12/10/89\ \ \ \ \ author: margreet sanders\\
Restricted rule to work only when VP is completely empty (not just when there 
is no head or predrel/VERBP). Easier for surface parser.
\item date: ../../..\ \ \ \ \ author:
\end{enumerate}
\item[* task:] To delete the VP when it does not dominate anything anymore
This transformation is necessary for the surface parser (so in analysis)
